<title>USA: FNB Financial predicts Q1 profit off 6 pct.</title>
<headline>FNB Financial predicts Q1 profit off 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>REIDSVILLE, N.C. 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>FNB Financial Service Corp, parent of First National Bank, said Thursday that earnings in the first quarter of 1997 would be six percent below the year-earlier period as a result of costs incurred in the opening of three new branches.</p>
<p>The company said, however, that it expected subsequent strong earnings growth, as loans have increased to record levels.</p>
</text>
